---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
---
<Site>
  <main id="main" class="wrap">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="headline">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Vibe coding, with standards.</p>
        <h1 id="headline">Vibe coding<br />for adults.</h1>
        <p class="premise">The fun part was never the problem.</p>
        <p class="intro">Keep the speed and possibility of a conversation. Add clear decisions, a real handoff, and a result that has been checked.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="https://kogen.dev">Meet Kogen <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a href="#the-approach">The approach <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="kit"><img src="/brand/kogen-kit-black.svg" alt="The Kogen model kit: purposeful parts held in a frame, ready to assemble." width="420" height="434" fetchpriority="high" /></figure>
    </section>

    <section class="argument" id="the-approach" aria-labelledby="argument-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Keep the judgment.</p><h2 id="argument-title">Lose the<br class="wide" /> supervision.</h2></div>
      <div class="argument-copy"><p>Getting something on screen is a good start. Knowing it does what you meant, handles the awkward cases, and fits the rest of the software takes more.</p><p>That work belongs in the build. Kogen’s approach is to shape the feature with you, get your approval, then carry the implementation through checks, independent review, and rework.</p><p>You decide what matters. The builder still has to show its work.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="process" aria-labelledby="process-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="process-title">A conversation.<br />With a clear handoff.</h2><p>Shape → Approve → Build → Commit</p></div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><span class="number">01</span><h3>Shape it.</h3><p>Work out the feature with Kogen: what changes, how it should work, and which product, UX, or technical decisions matter.</p></li>
        <li><span class="number">02</span><h3>Approve it.</h3><p>The Intent captures the feature, its boundaries, and the evidence required. You approve it before the Build starts.</p></li>
        <li><span class="number">03</span><h3>Leave the build.</h3><p>Kogen implements, checks, independently reviews, and reworks the result. The builder’s own claim of success is not enough.</p></li>
        <li><span class="number">04</span><h3>Keep the result.</h3><p>A Commit is the checked and accepted implementation of one Intent. A failed or stopped Build is not a delivered feature.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="closing" aria-labelledby="kogen-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">The project behind the approach</p><h2 id="kogen-title">Shape the feature.<br />Leave the build to Kogen.</h2><p>Make the product and UX decisions that define the feature. Specify technical decisions when they matter. Kogen handles the implementation, checking, independent review, rework, and resulting commit.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://kogen.dev">Meet Kogen <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="https://github.com/KogenAI/kogen">View source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><p class="availability">For current capabilities and availability, visit <a href="https://kogen.dev">kogen.dev</a>.</p></div>
      <a class="origins" href="https://kogen.dev/origins/">Every project<br />has a backstory.<span>Read the origins <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
    </section>
  </main>
</Site>
